7. READINESS CHECK AND FAILURE DETAILS
--------------------------------------------------

When Check Readiness is clicked:
- Check the current calculation, sector, and scenario.
- Display “Checking Readiness” with a loading indicator.
- Prevent duplicate requests.
- Keep Run Calculation disabled.

When readiness passes:
- Show green “Ready to Calculate”.
- Show:
  “All required configurations and inputs are available.”
- Display the successful check timestamp.
- Enable Run Calculation only when no active execution exists for the
  selected context.

When readiness fails:
- Show red “Not Ready”.
- Keep Run Calculation disabled.
- Automatically expand a Readiness Issues panel below Calculation Context.
- Show the actual failed prerequisites.

Columns:
Check | Failure Reason | Suggested Action

Illustrative issue types:
- Tax rate configuration missing for selected sector.
- Required forecast inputs not loaded.
- Scenario configuration incomplete.
- Sector/entity mapping incomplete.

Use backend-provided failures, not hardcoded examples.

Suggested actions should link to existing configuration screens only when
valid routes and permissions are available. Otherwise show explanatory text.

Provide “Check Again” after issues are resolved.

If the readiness request itself fails:
- Display “Readiness Check Unavailable” or “Check Failed”.
- Explain that readiness could not be verified.
- Keep Run Calculation disabled.
- Do not incorrectly report configuration failures or successful readiness.

Readiness errors must remain visible in the panel, not only in a toast.

--------------------------------------------------
8. STARTING A CALCULATION
--------------------------------------------------

Enable Run Calculation only when:
- Required context selections are valid.
- Readiness has passed for that exact context.
- No conflicting execution is already active.
- No start request is currently being submitted.

When clicked:
- Submit the execution request.
- Show a “Starting Calculation” state.
- Prevent duplicate clicks.
- Display the returned run ID and actual execution state.
- Update the top stepper as backend status becomes available.

If the start request fails:
- Show the actual error.
- Do not fabricate a run ID or running state.
- Restore the appropriate action state based on current readiness.

If the backend rejects execution because prerequisites changed:
- Invalidate readiness.
- Show the returned issues.
- Require readiness to pass again.

