- Expand the error details.
- Display the actual failure reason.
- Show corrective guidance if available.
- Keep later stages unexecuted.
- Do not show successful completion.

Status refresh failures:
- Preserve the last known execution state.
- Display “Unable to refresh status”.
- Show the last successful update timestamp.
- Do not treat a failed status request as a failed calculation.

Use backend-supported push updates or configurable polling.
Stop polling after a terminal execution state.
Clean up polling/subscriptions when leaving the relevant view.

